{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Issues in the Workplace", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What About Adam?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe  necessity, duty, advice, or strong disapproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to progress ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bimprove or \u200bdevelop in \u200bskills, \u200bknowledge, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is progressing quite well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you can use to talk about your work. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "layout", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way in which something is arranged", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He gave a presentation on our current office layout.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put into", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time or use energy doing something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He put a lot of research into it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to disrupt", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to prevent something from continuing by causing problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Adam has been disrupting the work of others. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disturbance", "type": "name"}, {"content": " something that interrupts what you are doing, or the act of making this happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It came across as more of a disturbance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bring something to somebody's attention", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tell someone about something such as a problem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why was this not brought to my attention earlier, Boris?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take care of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to deal with something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Consider it taken care of.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Interpreting the Meaning of What Has Been Said", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to clarify or emphasize what you have understood from an oral or written text, you can use certain phrases such as the following:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I infer from your e-mail that ... </br> The only possible inference is that ... </br> Your comments imply that ... </br> From the tone of your voice, I conclude that ... </br> Judging by your reply, you ... </br> What you are saying in so many words is that ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These phrases are quite formal and therefore useful in a workplace setting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "From the tone of your voice, I conclude this is a serious matter. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Judging by your reply, you don't seem to share my opinion on this matter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Your comments imply that is an urgent matter that needs to be addressed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What you are saying in so many words is that I need to have a talk with him.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reported Structures: Types of Clauses: That and Wh-Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to refer to what other people said or wrote, you can use report verbs with certain types of clauses.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class = \"bullet\"> You use <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\"> that-clauses</span></span> to report statements:</br>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">John suggested <span class=\"strong\">that we should go</span> to the movie.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"bullet\"> You can use <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">that-clauses</span></span> to report statements that include <span class=\"underline\"><span class=\"italic\">wh-clauses</span></span>: <br> For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> He remembered <span class=\"strong\">that what was weird</span> was that the man refused to leave his business card. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class = \"bullet\"> You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">wh-clauses</span></span> to report questions: </br>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">My manager asked me <span class=\"strong\">when I was thinking</span> of taking a vacation. </br>Their team wanted to know <span class=\"strong\">where we had put</span> the project files.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I thought you said that he was doing well. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As you are aware, he suggested that this should be improved. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He believes that what he was doing was helping others but it came across as more of a disturbance in the office. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We implied that is an urgent matter that needs to be addressed. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about an issue related to work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I interpret what someone has said.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about events and actions related to the workplace with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a dialogue (15-20 lines) between two co-workers discussing a matter in the workplace. Report on what has happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use certain phrases to interpret what the other has said.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading your dialogue aloud.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about solving problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can report facts about events or actions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about my work responsibilities.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What do you do when dealing with a difficult coworker?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How do you solve the issue? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " How will the situation be taken care of? ", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nBoris talks to Denise about Adam's behavior <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">as of late</span>. What's he been doing?\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": 